"b48da8241059d79c","eab14b56483283eb","09bd652341a96d42","9a1f3bffdb9409b3","2c236d7e10513002","1119e7204233f5b6","de789b6376b3ebdf","a0dfd09eecc05ac4","dc27b22c59e8b4a9","60a72a3082c84045","8222daec271f8e6f","44dad076011e62c1","eb12574abea1749d"],"findings":"The change is mostly lean. These are the five suggestions I'd make. I read the code but didn't run anything, so all of them are **read**, not verified.\n\n1. **Group `idem-rerun`, `src/commands/reviews.ts` (the decide-file loop in `run`).** The `fresh` set, the `filter` over `records[i]` and the `records[records.length-1]` marker check are indirect.\n   - Records are shared objects, so the code tracks which ones were written and then maps back to entries by index.\n   - Move the loop next to `prepareBatch` as `applyBatch(holders, records)`. It would return `{ decisions, marked, written, skipped }`.\n   - Count `decisions` and `marked` while iterating, from `todo.filter(r => !r.complete)` and `todo.some(r => r.complete)`.\n   - That removes the `fresh` set and the index arithmetic.\n   - It also finishes the TODO item \"move the `--decide-file` branch out of `run`\", which `prepareBatch` only half does.\n   - Small, about 15 lines.\n\n2. **Group `template-skip`/`dup-refs`, `scan` in `src/findings.ts`.** `headingRefs` is redundant.\n   - `withItems` only ever holds section labels. Item refs like `1.1` never go in it.\n   - `found` only has a bare label as a key when a numbered heading added it.\n   - So `headingsWithItems` can just be `withItems`. Drop `headingRefs` and the `new Set([...headingRefs].filter(...))` copy.\n   - Tiny, 3 lines.\n\n3. **Group `dup-refs`, `stripLabel`.** It now has two parallel paths, the new suffix regex and the old hand-written digit loop. One regex does both: `/^\\*\\*\\[\\d{1,3}[a-z]{0,2}(\\.\\d{1,6})?\\]\\*\\* */`.\n   - The old loop accepts any run of digits and dots up to 17 characters, for example `[1.2.3]`. A regex would be stricter, so I'd check that the existing label-idempotency tests still pass.\n   - It is slightly riskier than the others, but it removes a special case.\n   - Small.\n\n4. **Group `write-cap`.** `JSON.stringify(r).length + 1` counts UTF-16 code units, not bytes.\n   - The constant, the message and the README all say KiB of bytes. Non-ASCII text would be undercounted by up to 3x.\n   - Use `Buffer.byteLength(JSON.stringify(r)) + 1` so the code matches its name and message.\n   - One line.\n   - The 9-line comment on `MAX_BATCH_WRITE_BYTES` could shrink to about 3 lines. It restates the rationale already in the README and the commit.\n\n5. **Group `dup-refs`, `SUFFIXES`/`sectionLabel`/`compareRefs`.** The 701-entry precomputed table, plus `Math.min(seen, length) - 1`, is more machinery than needed.\n   - A small function can produce the suffix directly: `seen<=25 → letter`, otherwise two letters from `(seen-26)`.\n   - `compareRefs` also builds key objects on every comparison, and `!` on the regex result relies on refs always matching. It could parse once per sort, or compare with `localeCompare` on `suf.length`.\n   - This is cosmetic, so it ranks last.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
